hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17753","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Said al-Jurayri, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Hanzala al-Tamimi al-Usayyidi the scribe who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we mentioned Paradise and the Fire until it was as if we saw with our eyes. Then I came to my family and children and laughed and played, and I remembered what we had been in. So I went out and met Abu Bakr and said: I have been hypocritical, I have been hypocritical. He said: We too do it. So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. He said: O Hanzala, if you were as you are with me, the angels would shake hands with you upon your beds, or upon your roads, or a word like this. Thus he said, meaning Sufyan. O Hanzala, an hour and an hour."
"17754","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Muraqqa ibn Sayfi, from Hanzala the scribe who said: We campaigned with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we passed by a slain woman with people gathered over her. He said: They made way for him. He said: She was not one to be fought. Then he said to a man: Go to Khalid ibn al-Walid and say to him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) orders you not to kill offspring nor a hireling."
"17755","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father who said: Al-Muraqqa ibn Sayfi ibn Rabah, the brother of Hanzala the scribe, informed me. My grandfather informed me that he went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then he mentioned the hadith."
"17756","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad who said: Al-Muraqqa ibn Sayfi ibn Rabah informed me that his grandfather Rabah ibn Rabi informed him. Then he mentioned the hadith."
